AB  - In this article, we present a scenario-driven artificial intelligence (AI) + virtual reality (VR) language practice platform designed to support immersive role-play and open-ended spoken interaction for L2 speaking practice. The system combines interactive VR scenarios, large-language-model-driven real-time conversations, a block-based scenario authoring tool for customizing practice content, reflective analytics derived from conversation logs, and a privacy-aware social layer for peer support. The platform integrates the OpenAI GPT-4 Realtime application programming interface (API) within the Unity 3D engine to enable low-latency conversational interaction in immersive environments. We report a technical feasibility assessment and a formative usability evaluation. In a study with 30 learners, the platform achieved a mean System Usability Scale score of 73.25, a p95 frame time of 10.69 ms, and an average AI response latency of 0.77 s. These results provide initial evidence that the proposed design can deliver responsive AI-mediated dialogue and a usable end-to-end experience for scenario-based practice. We conclude with design tradeoffs, key limitations of the current short-term evaluation, and directions for learning-oriented and longitudinal studies.
ER  - 

