AB  - This paper introduces an innovative technical form to enhance visiting experiences that respect the user perspectives about cultural heritage and the integrity of cultural contents. We curate an interactive art exhibition, CanalWalk, using an autobiographical design approach to reconstruct cultural heritage through co-creation. Our design integrates generative AI and VR sketches to reinterpret cultural landmarks along the Grand Canal. CanalWalk combines a series of interactive mechanisms to foster cultural exploration, self-expression and social communication in visits. This research demonstrates the potential of combining generative design, spatial storytelling, and social VR to represent cultural heritage.
