AB  - Digital transformation in education demands new approaches that transcend the passivity of traditional methods. In the context of historical preservation, display cases limit user interaction, restricting active learning. This work proposes an engineering framework for the rapid development of Narrative Virtual Museums, using Virtual Reality (VR) to create high-fidelity psychophysical experiences. The case study focuses on the Brazilian Expeditionary Force (FEB), applying immersive technologies to overcome barriers to access and engagement. The methodology integrates human-centered design principles with a Generative Artificial Intelligence (AI)-assisted prototyping pipeline, optimizing the creation of assets, scripts, and programming logic in Unreal Engine 5. The resulting system validates the ability of immersive systems engineering to generate Presence and empathy, solving the historical trade-off between convenience and verisimilitude in remote environments. This model offers a scalable solution for sustainable innovation in Digital Humanities. Keywords: Digital Transformation; AI-Assisted Engineering; Virtual Reality; Virtual Museum; Presence; Human-Centered Design.
