AB  - Instigating the deep integration of BioGPT and diffusion model for zero-shot and few-shot classification of breast cancer subtypes which is rare. It is highly significant for human society because it addresses several critical challenges. The diagnosis of rare breast cancer subtypes is hampered by the scarcity of data in histopathology. We propose the first framework that integrates BioGPT deeply with diffusion models via crossattention, embedding biomedical knowledge directly into the generative process. This produces high-fidelity synthetic images across 16 subtypes, that mainly includes invasive micro papillary carcinoma. Synthetic data is proven to be highly effective. It improved the classification accuracy to 96.8% with an additional boost of 3.25% when augmentation is done in real slides. Medically aware generative AI can help bridge the data scarcity gap, providing new tools to support more accurate and equitable cancer diagnosis, particularly in rare and hard-to-detect cases.
